    "harness": "Every cell was re-measured after three harness fixes that move the number: the HTTP client read responses 10 KiB at a time; warmup converged on a reduced-step shape instead of the measured one; and measured requests carried a perf dump only sglang was asked for (+233ms on the first request, +1.35% on the rest). The earlier cells were discarded rather than merged.",
    "stacks": "Dependency versions, which this run's artifacts predate recording: vLLM-Omni torch 2.13.0 / transformers 5.14.1 / diffusers 0.40.0 / huggingface_hub 1.31.0; LightX2V torch 2.11.0 / transformers 5.17.0 / diffusers 0.40.0 / hub 1.31.0; trtllm-visual torch 2.12.0 / transformers 5.5.4 / diffusers 0.39.0 / hub 1.16.1. LightX2V moved off a transformers<5 pin during this round, which is what un-broke its FLUX.2 cell.",
    "jitter": "This box produces an occasional slow request in any framework -- 2 in 40 at +21% and +34% with no instrumentation at all. Cells whose repeats spread 25% or more are marked and their samples listed.",
    "zimage_sglang": "The Z-Image-Turbo sglang cell is published as measured (0.678s, samples 0.68/0.474/0.678/0.68/0.673) but is NOT reproducible: 22 later measurements across 20 freshly started servers on this same box, with the same command, all landed at 0.467-0.487s, which would win the cell rather than lose it. The 0.678s mode has been observed once. Treat this cell as an unexplained outlier pending a controlled re-measure, not as sglang's Z-Image latency."
